PartialFillSettler_fill
├── when block.timestamp is greater than order.fillDeadline
│   └── it should revert with FillAfterDeadline
├── when orderStatus is Settled or Refunded or Cancelled
│   └── it should revert with OrderInTerminalState
├── when orderData.allowPartialFills is false
│   └── it should revert with InconsistentIntent
├── when orderData.srcCstToken equals orderData.premiumToken
│   └── it should revert with InvalidOrderTokenPair
├── when orderData.exclusiveFiller is set AND msg.sender is not that address
│   └── it should revert with NotExclusiveFiller
├── when orderData.exclusiveFiller is set AND msg.sender is that address
│   └── it should accept the fill
├── when orderData.minFillSize is non-zero AND output.amount is less than minFillSize
│   └── it should revert with BelowMinFillSize
├── when orderData.minFillSize is non-zero AND rollover fill leaves residual strictly between zero and minFillSize
│   └── it should revert with ResidualTruncates
├── when orderData.minFillSize is non-zero AND rollover fill closes the order exactly
│   └── it should accept the fill regardless of residual-below-minFillSize rule
├── when orderData.minFillSize is non-zero AND caller fills the premium leg with premium output.amount below minFillSize
│   └── it should admit the premium leg (AS-19 is rollover-leg only)
├── when collateralAsset decimals are 6 AND rollover output.amount is aligned to the decimal offset
│   └── it should accept the fill (AS-20 gate admits)
├── when collateralAsset decimals are 6 AND rollover output.amount is not aligned to the decimal offset
│   └── it should revert with DecimalTruncates
├── when collateralAsset decimals are 18 or greater
│   └── it should be a no-op regardless of rollover output.amount modulo (AS-20 early return)
├── when intent hash mismatches orderData.cellarIntentHash
│   └── it should revert with IntentNotBoundToOrder
├── when fillerData.outputIndex is 0 (rollover leg)
│   ├── when targetFiller is not equal to msg.sender
│   │   └── it should revert with TargetFillerMismatch
│   ├── when destination is the zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with InvalidDestination
│   ├── when f.srcCstProvided is not zero for the caller
│   │   └── it should revert with AlreadyFilledByFiller
│   ├── when cumulative plus output.amount exceeds orderSize
│   │   └── it should bubble OverfillCeiling from the cellar
│   ├── when the cellar returns actualRolled equal to zero
│   │   └── it should revert with ZeroRollover
│   ├── when allowUnderfill is false AND actualRolled is less than output.amount
│   │   └── it should bubble UnderfillNotAllowed from the cellar
│   ├── when actualRolled equals output.amount
│   │   └── it should write f.srcCstProvided, f.dstCstProduced, f.destination, increment totalDstCstEscrowed and participantCount, pull leftover srcCST to msg.sender, and leave orderStatus unchanged
│   ├── when actualRolled is less than output.amount AND allowUnderfill is true
│   │   └── it should write the same filler state with the smaller srcCstProvided
│   ├── when this fill brings cumulative to orderSize exactly
│   │   └── it should observe the cellar flip the phase-0 terminal bit and delete rolled[d]
│   ├── when a subsequent rollover fill is attempted after phase-0 terminal
│   │   └── it should bubble PhaseAlreadyConsumed from the cellar
│   ├── when two concurrent fills race past the ceiling
│   │   └── it should revert with OverfillCeiling for the losing fill (linearised via rolled[])
│   └── when dstCstProduced exceeds what would fit in uint128
│       └── it should record FillerRollover.dstCstProduced at full uint256 width without narrowing (PR 3 / #53)
├── when fillerData.outputIndex is 1 (premium leg)
│   ├── when f.srcCstProvided is zero for targetFiller
│   │   └── it should revert with NoRolloverLegForFiller
│   ├── when f.premiumSettled is already true
│   │   └── it should revert with AlreadySettled
│   ├── when debitFrom equals msg.sender
│   │   └── it should accept the authorization
│   ├── when debitFrom is not msg.sender AND isOperator is true
│   │   └── it should accept the authorization
│   ├── when debitFrom is not msg.sender AND isOperator is false
│   │   └── it should revert with UnauthorizedDebitFrom
│   ├── when msg.sender is not targetFiller
│   │   └── it should accept (anyone may settle another filler's premium)
│   ├── when all authorization passes
│   │   ├── it should compute premium as ceilDiv of f.dstCstProduced multiplied by minPremiumPerShare divided by 1e18
│   │   ├── it should debit via ERC6909.settle
│   │   ├── it should flip f.premiumSettled to true and leave orderStatus unchanged
│   │   └── it should forward factory.executeIntentHooks with phase 1 and filler equal to targetFiller
│   ├── when the cellar phase-1 premiumHooks revert after the ERC-6909 debit
│   │   └── it should emit PremiumHooksReverted, leave ERC-6909 debit and f.premiumSettled committed, and not revert (AS-10 / #58)
│   ├── when premiumFiredFor[d][targetFiller] is already true
│   │   └── it should bubble PremiumAlreadyFiredForFiller from the cellar
│   └── when factory.originatingSettler() is not intent.settler
│       └── it should emit PremiumHooksReverted and latch f.premiumSettled (cellar-side revert caught by the AS-10 try/catch)
├── when fillerData.outputIndex is neither 0 nor 1
│   └── it should revert with InvalidOutputIndex
└── when a reentrant fill is attempted from the dstCST transferCallback
    └── it should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall
